you, take a second to hit subscribe; it

108
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:45,006
really helps this new channel reach more curious

109
00:04:44,856 --> 00:04:45,006
minds.

110
00:04:45,706 --> 00:04:49,070
Okay, an apple hits the ground and stops.

111
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:54,970
What about the Moon?

112
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:56,290
It's moving at over three thousand six hundred

113
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:56,660
kilometers per hour, every single second, for billions

114
00:04:56,510 --> 00:04:56,710
of years.

115
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:59,480
Why doesn't that drain Earth's energy?

116
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:03,530
In sixteen eighty-seven, Isaac Newton explained orbits with

117
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:05,360
a brilliant thought experiment.

118
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,690
Imagine firing a cannonball from the top of

119
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:10,320
an impossibly tall mountain.

120
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:13,330
Fire it slowly, and gravity pulls it down

121
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,340
to the ground.

122
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:17,600
Fire it faster, and it travels farther before

123
00:05:17,450 --> 00:05:18,190
landing.

124
00:05:18,470 --> 00:05:21,100
Fire it fast enough, about seven point eight

125
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:24,970
kilometers per second, and the cannonball still falls

126
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:28,210
toward Earth, but the curved planet drops away

127
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:30,380
beneath it at the exact same rate.

128
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:34,150
It falls forever, and keeps missing the ground.

129
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,730
Now look at the geometry of a circular

130
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:37,100
orbit.

131
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:40,510
The Moon's motion points straight ahead, while Earth's

132
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:44,280
gravity pulls straight inward at a perfect ninety-degree

133
00:05:44,130 --> 00:05:44,870
angle.

134
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:47,490
Because gravity pulls sideways to the motion, it

135
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:50,500
changes the Moon's direction, never its speed.

136
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:54,430
Zero change in speed means zero net energy

137
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:56,157
added, and zero fuel burned.

138
00:05:56,857 --> 00:06:00,380
For more than two hundred years, Newton's picture

139
00:06:00,230 --> 00:06:02,990
worked so well that we sent rockets into

140
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,170
space with it.

141
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:07,480
Yet Newton himself admitted he had no idea

142
00:06:07,330 --> 00:06:10,720
how Earth reached across empty space to yank

143
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:11,530
on the Moon.

144
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:16,100
Then, in nineteen fifteen, Albert Einstein flipped the

145
00:06:15,950 --> 00:06:18,220
entire mystery upside down.

146
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:21,880
Einstein realized that gravity doesn't need a power

147
00:06:21,730 --> 00:06:25,070
source because gravity isn't a pulling force at

148
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,670
all.

149
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:30,710
Instead, mass and energy bend the four-dimensional fabric

150
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,870
of space and time itself.

151
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:36,070
Think of a marble rolling across a smooth,

152
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,225
curved bowl.

153
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:39,860
Nobody is pulling the marble with a string,

154
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:42,160
and no engine is pushing it around the

155
00:06:42,010 --> 00:06:42,670
rim.

156
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:45,850
The marble is simply following the straightest possible

157
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:49,870
path, called a geodesic, through curved geometry.

158
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:53,900
Earth doesn't spend energy pulling the Moon, any

159
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:56,290
more than a hill spends energy making a

160
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,270
road curve.

161
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,540
Mass simply tells spacetime how to curve, and

162
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:03,770
curved spacetime tells matter how to move.

163
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:07,390
Once the shape is there, geometry takes zero

164
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,001
fuel to exist.

165
00:07:08,701 --> 00:07:11,720
Now, if you're paying close attention, you might

166
00:07:11,570 --> 00:07:15,380
ask a sharp question: doesn't gravity ever transfer

167
00:07:15,230 --> 00:07:16,470
real energy?

168
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:19,520
After all, the Moon's gravity lifts billions of

169
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:21,850
tons of ocean water into high and low

170
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,320
tides twice every day.

171
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:25,560
Where does that energy come from?

172
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:29,070
That's the exact right question, and the answer

173
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:31,190
proves nature never cheats.

174
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:34,080
The Moon's gravity doesn't create tidal energy out

175
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:34,530
of thin air.

176
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,390
Instead, the friction of sloshing oceans acts like

177
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,480
a giant brake pad on Earth's rotation.

178
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:44,380
Every century, Earth's spin slows down by about

179
00:07:44,403 --> 00:07:47,690
one point seven milliseconds, and that stolen rotational

180
00:07:47,670 --> 00:07:51,020
energy pushes the Moon three point eight centimeters

181
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:53,970
farther away from us every single year.

182
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:56,880
Even in deep space, there's a tiny energy

183
00:07:56,730 --> 00:07:57,170
leak.

184
00:07:57,430 --> 00:08:00,270
When massive objects like two black holes orbit

185
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:03,330
each other, they stir ripples in spacetime called

186
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:07,167
gravitational waves, first detected by LIGO in twenty

187
00:08:07,318 --> 00:08:07,718
fifteen.

188
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:11,430
Those waves carry energy away, causing the black

189
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,640
holes to spiral closer until they collide.

190
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:17,490
Even for Einstein, the energy bill is always

191
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:17,896
paid in full.

192
00:08:18,596 --> 00:08:21,770
So whenever you see gravity doing real work,

193
00:08:21,690 --> 00:08:24,870
whether it's water crashing through a hydroelectric dam

194
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:27,590
to light up a city, or an asteroid

195
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:31,560
slamming into a planet, someone always paid the

196
00:08:31,410 --> 00:08:33,120
energy bill up front.

197
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:36,100
In a hydroelectric dam, the Sun paid the

198
00:08:35,950 --> 00:08:38,890
bill by heating the oceans and lifting water

199
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:40,430
vapor up into mountain clouds.

200
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:43,630
Gravity simply cashed the check on the way

201
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,670
back down.

202
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:47,480
And the deep spacetime bowl around Earth?

203
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:49,740
That was paid for four and a half

204
00:08:49,590 --> 00:08:52,590
billion years ago, when a vast cloud of

205
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:58,040
ancient stardust collapsed inward, turning its gravitational potential

206
00:08:57,890 --> 00:09:00,856
energy into the blazing heat that forged our

207
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:00,856
planet.

208
00:09:01,556 --> 00:09:03,770
So the next time you drop your keys,

209
00:09:03,970 --> 00:09:06,710
or look up at the Moon hanging silently

210
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:09,550
in the night sky, remember why it never

211
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,170
runs out of battery.

212
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:14,120
Gravity doesn't need fuel to hold the universe

213
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:18,520
together, because holding still does zero work, and

214
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:22,070
bending spacetime isn't an engine burning energy.

215
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:25,220
It's simply the shape of the universe itself.

